'''Quiggold''' was a male [[Gabdorin]] [[pirate]] and [[Buccaneer/Canon|buccaneer]] from [[Gabdor]] and the [[First Mate]] of [[Captain]] [[Sidon Ithano]]'s [[Sidon Ithano's pirate crew|crew]].

==Biography==
===Early life and pirate career===
[[File:Meson_Martinet_TFA.png|thumb|left|250px|Quiggold boards the ''Meson Martinet'' behind Finn.]]
Quiggold had lived comfortably at [[Cloudshape Falls]] on [[Alderaan]] from his cozy rooms, deceiving the naive stashing [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]]. The [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] eventually caught up with him, and Quiggold was aboard an [[Unidentified Imperial prisoner shuttle|Imperial prisoner shuttle]], leaving luxurious Alderaan for some lunar work camp in a remote [[star system|system]], accused of "financial creativity." He had backups before the [[Imperial Security Bureau|ISB]] had frozen his account, but he must get out of [[prison]] first.<ref name="Sinister Secret of the Binary Star">{{InsiderCite|234|Galactic Tales: The Crimson Corsair and the Sinister Secret of the Binary Star}}</ref> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas Updated">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> the [[Death Star]], a [[moon]]-sized [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|space station]], entered the [[Alderaan system|system]]<ref name="Sinister Secret of the Binary Star" /> and used its massive [[superlaser]] to [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroy]] the [[planet]] Alderaan, killing billions of [[Alderaanian]]s<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> and creating an abrupt [[gravity]] well that caused the [[shuttle]] to spin out of control.<ref name="Sinister Secret of the Binary Star" />

Quiggold was a male [[Gabdorin]] [[pirate]]<ref name="Lost Treasure" /> and [[Buccaneer/Canon|buccaneer]]<ref name="GoH news">{{EA|url=games/starwars/galaxy-of-heroes/news/kit-reveal-quiggold|text=Kit Reveal: Quiggold}}</ref> who served in a [[Sidon Ithano's pirate crew|pirate crew]] led by [[Captain]] [[Sidon Ithano]]. Hailing from [[Gabdor]], he was Ithano's [[First Mate]]. The crew operated primarily in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] in the decades after the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Quiggold was part of a mission in which Ithano hunted for a possible lost shipment of [[kyber crystal]]s that was originally meant to be delivered to [[Count]] [[Dooku]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. He and the rest of the crew ended up finding a [[clone trooper]] frozen in stasis named [[Kix]] and locations to long-forgotten former [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] bases.<ref name="Lost Treasure" />

Quiggold also accompanied Captain Ithano on a visit to [[Takodana Castle]] [[34 ABY|thirty years after]] the [[Battle of Endor]], where a fugitive [[First Order]] defector named [[Finn]] offered to join their crew in exchange for safe passage into the Outer Rim, away from the First Order's reach. Shortly before they could depart however, the First Order used the [[Starkiller Base]] [[superweapon]] to [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroy]] the [[New Republic]] [[Hosnian system]] and the former [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] returned back to the castle to watch the event with many other patrons. Shortly afterwards the First Order [[Battle of Takodana|attacked]] Takodana Castle in search for the [[Resistance]] [[Astromech droid]] [[BB-8]].<ref name="TFA" />

==Personality and traits==
Quiggold had brown skin and [[eye]]s and had a peg [[Limb|leg]] fashioned from a [[fuel funnel]].<ref name="DB" /> Between himself and Sidon Ithano, Quiggold did most of the talking.<ref name="Adventures12">[[Star Wars Adventures 12 (magazine)|''Star Wars Adventures'' 12]]</ref>

==Equipment==
Quiggold wore a simple green-brown hood and carried a set of [[prayer beads]] fashioned from [[hyperdrive plotter pin]]s.<ref name="DB" /> In battle he often used a [[heavy repeater cannon]] nicknamed [[Deck Sweeper]].<ref name="GoH news" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|This one has the ability to do loads of movement performed in real time using what we call a performance delivery system, that allows the person whose operating this to act and talk and deliver a set of lines.|Neal Scanlan, on Quiggold's costume in the "Crafting Creatures" featurette|<ref name="Crafting">{{HomeVideoCite|film=7|featurette=Crafting Creatures}}</ref>}}
[[File:Quiggold_DB.png|thumb|right|180px|Scott Richardson set in the Quiggold costume]]
Quiggold first appeared in the short story "[[The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku]]," which was written by [[Landry Q. Walker]] and released as the ''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'' multi-media campaign leading into the release of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] in [[2015]]. The character then made a minor appearance in the film itself played by real-life leg amputee [[Scott Richardson (real person)|Scott Richardson]], and was controlled and voiced by key animatronic designer [[Christopher Clarke|Chris Clarke]] with additional cover provided by Patrick Comerford. The mask of the Quiggold costume was an animatronic that allowed Clarke to manipulate the character's facial expression using a performance delivery system while delivering his lines. Richardson expressed interest in return for [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']],<ref name="starwarsinterviews">{{WebCite|url=https://starwarsinterviews.com/sequel-trilogy/episode-vii-the-force-awakens/scott-richardson-quiggold|text=Scott Richardson (Quiggold)|author=[[Dennis Pellegrom]]|date=2016-12|work=[[Star Wars Interviews]]|archivedate=20230131003129|nolive=1}}</ref> but neither he nor the character returned in that film.<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

